  "releaseNotes": "Refactor worker pools: simplify channels & metrics:\n      - Remove per-job enqueue timestamps and slow-job tracking, simplify channel payloads to plain delegates, and streamline priority-queue handling.\n      - Expose lightweight aggregate metrics (pending, active, totals, errors, dropped) via properties instead of heavy PoolStats/WorkerStats snapshots.\n      - Update SyncWorkerPool to use Channel<Action> and remove timestamp plumbing; adjust WorkerLoad layout and counters.\n      - LuciferWorker API/metrics surfaces adjusted (new properties for sync/async totals, pending, active, errors) and CanHandle logic simplified to only use fuzzy capacity checks.\n      - Also add dropped-job accounting when bounded channels reject writes and reduce telemetry/logging detail for high-latency cases.",
